> Thanks. Do you get the same errors when you install xsel?

Yes it does. 

The issue is the following:
1. It goes through https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/fe9e5d023e20304ad1bdfa1da53f3af452c72a00/pandas/io/clipboard/__init__.py#L511 with variable `HAS_DISPLAY == False`

it then executes https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/fe9e5d023e20304ad1bdfa1da53f3af452c72a00/pandas/io/clipboard/__init__.py#L581

and thus calls https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/fe9e5d023e20304ad1bdfa1da53f3af452c72a00/pandas/io/clipboard/__init__.py#L297

and raises the following exception:

```python
def init_no_clipboard():
    class ClipboardUnavailable:
        def __call__(self, *args, **kwargs):
            raise PyperclipException(EXCEPT_MSG)

        def __bool__(self) -> bool:
            return False

    return ClipboardUnavailable(), ClipboardUnavailable()
```
